@lang en
IMPORT `pvi-health-part5-claims`

-- PVI comprehensive health care rules: the assessment of one claim, putting the Parts together.
--
-- Layer 1, IS THE EVENT COVERED: `the grounds of refusal of` a claim lists every ground the Rules
-- give, each citing its clause: the premium (Part I clause 4); the benefit on the certificate
-- (Part III); the event in the insurance term (Part II "Tai nạn", Part I clause 10); the cost or
-- consequence within PVI's liability (Part I clause 10); the waiting period (Part III); the scope
-- of the benefit and its own exclusions (Part III); the general exclusions (Part IV). A claim is
-- covered when the list is empty.
--
-- Layer 2, HOW MUCH: the amount rules of Part III, paid only on a covered claim.
--
-- Layer 3, WHAT EACH PARTY MUST DO AND BY WHEN, is pvi-health-part5-claims.l4.

§ `The assessment of a claim`

§§ `Part I clause 10 — the cost or consequence within PVI's liability`

-- For the medical-expense benefits, the first day of the costs claimed must be within PVI's
-- liability (the days of a stay after it are dropped by the A.2 amount rule). For a death, the
-- date of death. Part III A.1.4 (iv) pays a death within one year of the accident after a Benefit 2
-- payment, which is read as prevailing over clause 10 (fork F21; finding X1). A permanent injury
-- is read as a consequence that arose with the accident, whenever it was determined (fork F21).
-- A cost BEFORE the start of the term is not clause 10's business: an event before the term fails
-- the term ground instead.
@ref PVI Rules Part I clause 10 (src:169-189)
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
      c IS A `A claim`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`clause 10 — after the last day of PVI's liability:` `the day` `, for` c MEANS
    `the day` GREATER THAN `clause 10 — the last day of PVI's liability under` (c's `the certificate`)

@ref PVI Rules Part I clause 10 (src:169-189); Part III A.1.4 (src:544-548)
GIVEN c IS A `A claim`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`clause 10 — the claim's cost or consequence arose after PVI's liability ended` c MEANS
    CONSIDER c's `the benefit claimed`
    WHEN `personal accident` THEN
        CONSIDER c's `the death or injury facts`'s `outcome`
        WHEN `death of the insured person` dd THEN
                `clause 10 — after the last day of PVI's liability:` dd `, for` c
            AND NOT (`A.1.4 (iv) — a death within one year after a Benefit 2 payment, on` dd `, for` c)
        OTHERWISE FALSE
    WHEN `death from illness` THEN
        CONSIDER c's `the death or injury facts`'s `outcome`
        WHEN `death of the insured person` dd THEN
            `clause 10 — after the last day of PVI's liability:` dd `, for` c
        OTHERWISE FALSE
    OTHERWISE
        `clause 10 — after the last day of PVI's liability:` (c's `the date of treatment`) `, for` c

@ref PVI Rules Part III A.1.4, fourth limb (src:544-548)
GIVEN `the date of death` IS A DATE
      c IS A `A claim`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`A.1.4 (iv) — a death within one year after a Benefit 2 payment, on` `the date of death` `, for` c MEANS
        c's `the death or injury facts`'s `already paid under Benefit 2 for the same accident` GREATER THAN 0
    AND `the date of death` AT MOST `add years` (c's `the date the event arose`) 1

§§ `Layer 1 — Is the event covered?`

GIVEN g IS A `A ground of refusal`
      p IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF `A ground of refusal`
`the ground` g `where` p MEANS
    IF p THEN LIST g ELSE EMPTY

@ref PVI Rules Parts I-IV
GIVEN c IS A `A claim`
GIVETH A LIST OF `A ground of refusal`
`the grounds of refusal of` c MEANS
    concat (LIST
        `the ground` `the premium was not paid in full and on time`
            `where` (`clause 4 — PVI is not liable because the premium was not paid in full and on time` (c's `the certificate`))
      , `the ground` `the benefit is not on the certificate`
            `where` (NOT (`the certificate carries the benefit claimed in` c))
      , `the ground` `the event did not arise in the insurance term`
            `where` (NOT (`the event arose in the insurance term` c))
      , `the ground` `the cost arose after PVI's liability ended`
            `where` (`clause 10 — the claim's cost or consequence arose after PVI's liability ended` c)
      , `the ground` `the event arose in the waiting period`
            `where` (NOT (`the event in` c `arose after a waiting period of` (`the waiting period in days for` c)))
      , `what the claim lacks for the scope of the benefit claimed` c
      , map (GIVEN n YIELD `excluded by Part IV item` n) (`the Part IV items engaged by` c))

@ref PVI Rules Parts I-IV
GIVEN c IS A `A claim`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the claim is covered` c MEANS
    null (`the grounds of refusal of` c)

§§ `Layer 2 — How much is payable?`

@ref PVI Rules Part III, with Part I clause 3 and Part II "Đồng chi trả", "Số tiền bảo hiểm"
GIVEN c IS A `A claim`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the amount PVI pays on` c MEANS
    IF   `the claim is covered` c
    THEN `the amount the benefit claimed pays on` c
    ELSE 0
